======== key= away from a $for body's direct child ========
refused: at the top level
  | <li key={self.id}>x</li>
  refusal.bx:5:5: error: key={ } names the identity of one row of a $for, so it belongs on a tag directly inside a $for body. Here it names nothing the differ can use
refused: on a grandchild of the body
  | $for row: int in self.rows { <ul><li key={row}>x</li></ul> }
  refusal.bx:5:38: error: key={ } names the identity of one row of a $for, so it belongs on a tag directly inside a $for body. Here it names nothing the differ can use
refused: on a component tag
  | <Hint key={self.id} />
  refusal.bx:5:7: error: key={ } names the identity of one row of a $for, so it belongs on a tag directly inside a $for body. Here it names nothing the differ can use
refused: inside an $if, not a $for
  | $if self.on { <li key={self.id}>x</li> }
  refusal.bx:5:19: error: key={ } names the identity of one row of a $for, so it belongs on a tag directly inside a $for body. Here it names nothing the differ can use
refused: two keys in one $for body
  | $for row: int in self.rows { <li key={row}>a</li><li key={row}>b</li> }
  refusal.bx:5:54: error: two key={ } in one $for body — a row has one identity, so put the key on the one tag that is the row
refused: key with no expression
  | <li key="1">x</li>
  refusal.bx:5:5: error: key needs an expression: key={row.id}
accepted: on a direct child of a $for body
accepted: a keyless $for is indexed instead

======== ref= on a component tag is an assignment ========
accepted: ref= on a component tag, written first
  | <Hint ref={self.panel} label={self.label} />
  partial class Refusal {
      pub override fn render(b: Builder) {
          b.component<Hint>(0, fn(_latte_c: Hint) {  // refusal.bx:5
              _latte_c.label = self.label
              self.panel = some(_latte_c)
          })
      }
  }
  
accepted: ref= on an element is still a Reference sink
  | <input ref={self.box} name="boxed" />
  partial class Refusal {
      pub override fn render(b: Builder) {
          b.open(0, "input")  // refusal.bx:5
          b.reference(1, fn(_latte_handle: Reference) { self.box = _latte_handle })
          b.attr(2, "name", "boxed")
          b.close()
      }
  }
  
refused: ref= still needs a place, not a call
  | <Hint ref={self.find()} />
  refusal.bx:5:7: error: ref={self.find()} is not a field to write the handle into — ref needs a place, such as ref={self.input}
refused: ref= still needs an expression
  | <Hint ref="x" />
  refusal.bx:5:7: error: ref needs an expression: ref={self.input}

======== a <beans> import that collides with the generated one ========
refused: Builder, imported again
  | <beans>
  | package pages
  | import {Builder} from latte
  | pub partial class Refusal extends Component { pub fn init() {} }
  | </beans>
  | <p>x</p>
  refusal.bx:3:1: error: the <beans> block imports Builder from latte, and the generated file already does — latte-bx writes `import {Builder, Callback, Component, FocusEvent, InputEvent, KeyboardEvent, MouseEvent, Reference, SubmitEvent} from latte` at the top of every file it makes, and two imports of one name is an error in a file you did not write. Remove this one
refused: two of them at once
  | <beans>
  | package pages
  | import {MouseEvent, InputEvent} from latte
  | pub partial class Refusal extends Component { pub fn init() {} }
  | </beans>
  | <p>x</p>
  refusal.bx:3:1: error: the <beans> block imports MouseEvent from latte, and the generated file already does — latte-bx writes `import {Builder, Callback, Component, FocusEvent, InputEvent, KeyboardEvent, MouseEvent, Reference, SubmitEvent} from latte` at the top of every file it makes, and two imports of one name is an error in a file you did not write. Remove this one
  refusal.bx:3:1: error: the <beans> block imports InputEvent from latte, and the generated file already does — latte-bx writes `import {Builder, Callback, Component, FocusEvent, InputEvent, KeyboardEvent, MouseEvent, Reference, SubmitEvent} from latte` at the top of every file it makes, and two imports of one name is an error in a file you did not write. Remove this one
refused: Component, which the class extends
  | <beans>
  | package pages
  | import {Component} from latte
  | pub partial class Refusal extends Component { pub fn init() {} }
  | </beans>
  | <p>x</p>
  refusal.bx:3:1: error: the <beans> block imports Component from latte, and the generated file already does — latte-bx writes `import {Builder, Callback, Component, FocusEvent, InputEvent, KeyboardEvent, MouseEvent, Reference, SubmitEvent} from latte` at the top of every file it makes, and two imports of one name is an error in a file you did not write. Remove this one
accepted: a latte name the generated line does not bind
accepted: the same name under an alias binds a different one
accepted: the same name from somewhere else is not a collision here

