refused: a generic component may not spell its type parameter
  | <beans>
  | package pages
  | pub partial class Refusal<T> extends Component { pub rows: List<T> = []; pub fn init() {} }
  | </beans>
  | $for row: T in self.rows { <p>x</p> }
  refusal.bx:5:1: error: a $for header spells T, and the generated half of a generic component may not — `partial class` may carry its type parameters on exactly one part, so latte-bx writes `partial class` with none and T is not a name it can use (probes/ANSWERS.md §4). Drop the annotation and let it be inferred, or move the code that needs T into the <beans> block
accepted: a generic component that lets the element type be inferred
accepted: a comment mentioning partial class is not a declaration

======== live, and the bind: shapes ========
refused: live on its own
  | <span live>$self.ticks</span>
  refusal.bx:5:7: error: a live subtree is not in this version — signals are W7, and marking a subtree live before they exist would compile to an ordinary render that never updates the way the attribute promises
refused: live with a value
  | <div live="yes">y</div>
  refusal.bx:5:6: error: a live subtree is not in this version — signals are W7, and marking a subtree live before they exist would compile to an ordinary render that never updates the way the attribute promises
refused: bind:value on a <select>
  | <select bind:value={self.choice}><option>a</option></select>
  refusal.bx:5:9: error: bind:value on a <select> cannot set the initial selection: a select's value is not an attribute, it is which <option> carries selected. Write selected={...} on the option and on:change={...} for the write-back
refused: bind:value on anything else
  | <p bind:value={self.note}>x</p>
  refusal.bx:5:4: error: bind:value works on an <input> and a <textarea>, and this is a <p>
refused: bind:checked away from an <input>
  | <select bind:checked={self.on}></select>
  refusal.bx:5:9: error: bind:checked works on an <input>, and this is a <select>
refused: bind:checked with a conversion
  | <input bind:checked.int={self.on} />
  refusal.bx:5:8: error: bind:checked takes no conversion — it is already a bool
refused: a bind: target latte does not have
  | <input bind:text={self.note} />
  refusal.bx:5:8: error: bind:text is not a binding latte has — the two are bind:value and bind:checked
refused: a conversion latte does not have
  | <input bind:value.date={self.note} />
  refusal.bx:5:8: error: bind:value.date is not a conversion latte has — the three are .int, .float and .bool
refused: bind: with no place
  | <input bind:value />
  refusal.bx:5:8: error: bind:value needs the field to bind: bind:value={self.note}
refused: a bind: place that is a call
  | <input bind:value={self.get()} />
  refusal.bx:5:8: error: bind:value={self.get()} is not a field to write back to — a binding needs a place, such as bind:value={self.note}
refused: bind: on a component tag
  | <Hint bind:value={self.note} />
  refusal.bx:5:7: error: bind:value is a two-way binding on a form control and Hint is a component — pass the value down as a parameter and take the change back through a Callback
refused: a <textarea> that binds AND has children
  | <textarea bind:value={self.note}>extra</textarea>
  refusal.bx:5:11: error: a <textarea> with bind:value has its value as its content, so it cannot have children as well — remove them, or drop the binding and write the text yourself
accepted: bind:value on an <input>
accepted: bind:value on a <textarea>
accepted: the three conversions
accepted: bind:checked on an <input>
accepted: a select with an explicit selected= and on:change

